{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The repair epoxies felt like natural follow-ups to my duct tape and vinyl cement purchases because they offer another way to mend damaged parts. I would choose the steel-reinforced epoxy for durable metal repairs today.",
    "The 6-inch NEIKO caliper connects directly to my hose clamp purchases: measuring hose and fitting diameters would help me select a suitable clamp, and the unit conversions would be useful."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The 12-inch caliper and infrared thermometer lack a clear use for me right now. An interest in practical repairs does not mean I currently need large measurements or temperature checks.",
    "The locking nuts require a need for particular sizes, and the flap discs require a matching grinder and grinding task. Neither need is established by my clamp and adhesive purchases, while the fabric shaver serves a different purpose altogether."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My purchases seem to have been treated as a broad interest in tools and hardware, when I choose supplies for specific repair tasks.",
    "My adhesive purchases support interest in repair epoxy, but they do not mean I want several alternative epoxies at once. Likewise, several calipers address the same potential measuring need."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The connection between measuring hose diameters and choosing clamps matters more to me than a tool simply belonging in a workshop.",
    "I distinguish between something that could be useful eventually and something I would choose today. Plastic repair putty and quick-setting epoxy fit my interests, but I would prioritize one general repair epoxy this time."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognized my practical repair interests but stretched them into tool needs I have not shown and several alternatives I would not buy together."
}"}
